Goal: Skeid can load the caller side of its config – names:, keys: (per-key policy, model access), client_auth: – from a PostgreSQL database instead of (or merged with) the YAML file. The database is owned by another application, which creates and revokes customer keys; Skeid only reads.

Constraints from the ADRs:
- Only customer key IDs (k_ + full SHA-1, ADR 0016) are stored, never keys (ADR 0003).
- Resolved at config load/reload, never per request (ADR 0008, 0020); refresh must be async (ADR 0005) – e.g. periodic reload or LISTEN/NOTIFY.
- Skeid defines the contract: the table/view shape it reads, so the owning application can provide a view. Generic, no knowledge of who owns the database.
- Usage already goes to PostgreSQL via UsageStore::DBI; same DSN should be usable.

First a design (ADR draft + config shape + table/view contract), no code. Open questions: precedence file vs database, what happens when the DB is unreachable at load/reload (keep last good set?), revocation latency.

ADR draft committed: docs/adr/0022-customer-keys-can-come-from-a-database-view.md (Status: proposed), commit b101c06 on branch worktree-k108-adr-customer-source (not pushed, not merged). Design: customer_source: section in YAML; contract = SELECT key_id, name, policy, models FROM <relation>, one row per active key id (row absent = revoked); rows validated before merge, rejected rows grant nothing and never fail a reload; file wins per key id; allowlist is a union, only when client_auth is declared; deny_tags/profiles/manifest stay file-only; background Mojo::Pg fetcher (poll + optional LISTEN/NOTIFY), never on the request path; keep the last good snapshot during an outage, optional max_stale_s; degraded fail-closed start; separate connection/role even with from_usage_store. Open questions: (1) Mojo::Pg vs hand-rolled DBD::Pg async; (2) degraded start vs refuse to start; (3) max_stale_s default 0 vs finite; (4) deny_tags/manifest per row (proposed no); (5) keep the display-only name column?; (6) DB names referenceable from the file (proposed no); (7) env-gated real-PG xt/ test?

Implemented ADR 0022 (accepted). Commits on local main: b101c06 (ADR draft), f12cb30 (ADR accepted + resolved questions + blocking-connect gap), 2eef8d6 (customer_source implementation, t/72-75, docs, Changes). prove -lr t/: Files=80, Tests=4968, PASS (after installing Langertha 0.503 + DBD::SQLite locally; 6 pre-existing env failures otherwise). Left: DBD::Pg connect blocks the loop up to connect_timeout_s -> k109; real Mojo::Pg fetcher never run against a real DB (manual procedure in examples/service/skeid.yaml). Not pushed.

